\\u{0301}\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so two strings that differ only by the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordering of those scalars would compare as equal:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let aboveBeforeBelow = \"\\u{0041}\\u{0301}\\u{0316}\"","let belowBeforeAbove = \"\\u{0041}\\u{0316}\\u{0301}\"","print(aboveBeforeBelow == belowBeforeAbove)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":1,"text":"Named and Unnamed Combining Classes","anchor":"Named-and-Unnamed-Combining-Classes","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Canonical combining classes are defined in the Unicode Standard as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integers in the range ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...254","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For convenience, the standard assigns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbolic names to a subset of these combining classes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"CanonicalCombiningClass","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"RawRepresentable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raw value of type ","type":"text"},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You can create instances of the type by using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the static members named after the symbolic names, or by using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(rawValue:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" initializer.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let overlayClass = Unicode.CanonicalCombiningClass(rawValue: 1)","let overlayClassIsOverlay = overlayClass == .overlay","\/\/ overlayClassIsOverlay == true"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"title":"Unicode.CanonicalCombiningClass","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ",